# Registry stub for the externally trained model SevenNet-0 (not trained in this paper).
entity:run-SevenNet-0 a mlips:MLIPRun ;
    rdfs:label "Training run of SevenNet-0 (842k parameters, trained on MPtrj)" ;
    mlips:appliesMethod entity:NequIP ;
    mlips:produces entity:model-SevenNet-0 .

entity:model-SevenNet-0 a mlips:TrainedModel ;
    rdfs:label "SevenNet-0 (842k parameters, trained on MPtrj)" .

###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results (Q11 inference-cost properties inline)
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The diagonal Fisher information matrix is computed once on 1,154,095
# low-loss MPtrj configurations on 10 NVIDIA A100 (80 GB) GPUs in about 4 h
# 15 min (about 40 A100 GPU-hours). Replay and reEWC cost about twice the
# CPU time of Vanilla and EWC fine-tuning (Table 1).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - All accuracy results are figure-only (violin plots of energy and force MAEs and softening scales, Figs. 4 and 5; composite losses E_RMSE + F_RMSE + 0.01 S_RMSE, Figs. 2, 3, 12, 13). The text gives only approximate validation RMSEs for EWC and reEWC (about 1 meV/atom, 70 meV/A, 1.5 kbar), which are not encoded.
# - The lower-learning-rate run uses one tenth of the 0.0001 peak learning rate; since the paper does not restate the value, no learning rate is attached to it. Diffusivity MPE/MAPE values and the quasi-melting WMAE (Figs. 6, 7) are not error metrics of the schema.
# - The Replay and reEWC runs also train on the Replay set (10% of MPtrj, or a Li-focused set in Fig. 3); only the LPSC fine-tuning set is attached as their data set.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kim2025forgetting.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
